Doom for Inferno — build plan
=============================

Goal: run shareware Doom (doom1.wad) under hosted emu, engine rewritten
in Limbo.  Reference spec: doomgeneric's 5-function platform seam
(DG_Init, DG_DrawFrame, DG_SleepMs, DG_GetTicksMs, DG_GetKey) — we port
the seam to Inferno and translate the engine body C -> Limbo.

Platform services available in-tree (verified):
  blit      Draw->Image.writepixels(dst, r, data), module/draw.m:190;
            data must match the screen's native format — hosted emu
            is 32bpp XRGB32 (emu/port/win-x11a.c forces depth 32)
  screen    Display.allocate(nil) then draw/writepixels on
            display.image (appl/cmd/wish.b path); no Tk, no wm needed
  clock     Sys->millisec(), Sys->sleep(), module/sys.m:141,153
  keys      /dev/keyboard + /dev/pointer readers
            (appl/cmd/wish.b spawn pattern)
  audio     /dev/audio + /dev/audioctl, enc pcm, rate 11025
            (emu/port/audio-tbls.c — exactly Doom's SFX rate)

Layout
------
  wad.m/wad.b      WAD container loader (module, reusable)
  video.m/video.b  XRGB32 framebuffer -> emu screen blit (module)
  rend.m/rend.b    renderer: palette, colormap, flats, textures,
                   vanilla column/span drawers (module)
  doom.b           main command; grows with each milestone
  doom1.wad        shareware IWAD (data, place in $ROOT or pass path)
  PLAN             this file

Milestones (each independently testable)
----------------------------------------
  [x] 1  WAD loader + directory dump + lump read     (doom -d)
  [x] 2  video path: 320x200 framebuffer blitted onto the emu
         screen via writepixels; measure fps
         (doom -t: xor-plasma, ~101 fps at 320x200 XRGB32;
         screen is win-x11a's forced 32bpp, so the framebuffer
         is XRGB32 BGRX, not RGB24 — RGB24 writes fail with
         "loadimage: insufficient data")
  [x] 3  renderer: COLORMAP + PLAYPAL, flats, walls
         (doom -r: vanilla R_DrawColumn/R_DrawSpan, eager
         texture compositing from patches, 49 fps full-screen
         STARTAN3 wall + FLOOR4_8 floor with light gradients)
  [ ] 4  map load: LINEDEFS/SECTORS/SIDEDEFS/VERTEXES,
         geometry structs as Limbo adts
  [ ] 5  game tics: player movement, mobj state tables,
         Doom's tick loop (35Hz) driven from Sys->millisec
  [ ] 6  input: /dev/keyboard + /dev/pointer -> event chan
         (wish.b spawn-reader pattern; Tk bind optional later)
  [ ] 7  SFX: Doom mixer (8 x 8-bit unsigned channels)
         -> /dev/audioctl "enc pcm" "rate 11025"
  [ ] 8  polish: menus, status bar, demo playback

Porting notes (C -> Limbo idioms)
---------------------------------
- ints are 32-bit signed: WAD LE decoding done byte-wise in wad.b;
  C casts like (int)(x >> 24) need care with sign extension
- C unions -> tagged pick adts; struct tables -> arrays of adts/refs
- GC is the enemy: preallocate framebuffer, mix buffer, mobj pools;
  never allocate in per-column / per-pixel loops
- Doom state tables (mobjstate_t[], states[], flags[]) map
  mechanically onto Limbo arrays; see doomdef.h / info.c
- strings: C char* lump names -> Limbo string, compare with ==
- Limbo `for` has no C-style single-condition form; use `for(;;)`
  with break, or `for(i := 0; i < n; i++)`
- `for (i := 0; ...)` declares i in the ENCLOSING block, not the
  for statement: two loops in one function cannot both use
  `i :=`; declare once, reassign with `=` in later loops
- adt method dispatch across modules needs BOTH the type import
  (`File: import wad;`) AND that module variable load-ed in the
  calling module — otherwise "module not loaded" at call time
- W_CheckNumForName is case-insensitive and searches the lump
  directory backwards (last match wins); wad.b find matches that
- COLORMAP row 0 is not a strict identity: 7 colors are remapped
  even at full light (vanilla quirk, not a loader bug)
- Limbo has no int64: FixedMul is done in 16-bit halves (rend.b)
  for an exact 64-bit intermediate

